  "composition_summary": "Drafted one class-22 pure-logic candidate pc-check-timeout-ms (name/description/content only) per the instruction. The body uses inputs.get for the raw candidate, treats missing and null as distinct invalid outcomes, rejects booleans and floats, enforces exact integer 0..7500 inclusive, and assigns result={valid,timeout_ms} on every outcome without exceptions or coercion. This is an unapproved offline-design draft using the target typed-inputs interface; it is not a submission or activation. No provider capabilities were observed (catalogue_revision and protocol_capabilities are null), so no prompt repair was justified; the conversation is preserved unchanged. The host sink supports class 22 name/description/content, so the payload is a supported constructor draft. Q1, observed behavior and human Q2 precede activation.",
